 result←object(State Text)arg;was;t;props;tunits;text;item;points;at;NL;colors
 result←⍬
 ⍝ 'Text' text r c [h w]                    ⍝? h/w clipping is not supported in Dyalog ⍝? Can we fake it with clipping code?
 ⍝ 'Text' ([n m ⍴] text r c [h w]) ...      ⍝? h/w clipping is not supported in Dyalog ⍝? Can we fake it with clipping code?

⍝? If the text is rotated, I assume the origin point (r,c) is the top-left leading-corner of the first character. Is (h,w) measured from that same point?
⍝? How would I specify (h,w) in APL+Win in various rotation quadrants, since it can stick out in any direction?
⍝? I assume that Dyalog uses the same (r,c) starting point, even when rotated?

 :If 0=≢arg ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Empty command is ignored
 :If 2>|≡arg ⋄ :OrIf (2=|≡arg)∧##.IsNum 1↓arg ⋄ arg←,⊂,arg ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ This looks like a single Text request - nest it
 NL←⎕UCS 13
 tunits←⊃##.Classes._supp.MyUnits State
 :If 1 ¯2∊⍨≡arg ⋄ arg←,⊂arg ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Make sure a single argument is enclosed
 arg←⊃,/,¨↓¨arg ⍝ If any items are matrices, split them into individual lines so we can process them sequentially
 props←StartObj'Text'
 colors←(⊂⍬)##.Classes._supp.color2¨State._color_ ⍝ Text background, foreground
 props,←⊂'FCol'(2⊃colors) ⍝ They'll always want a foreground color to write the text with
 props,←(1⊃State._mode)/⊂'BCol'(1⊃colors) ⍝ They may also want a background behind the text
 props,←(~1⊃State._mode)/⊂'BCol'(3⍴255) ⍝? Testing forced white background until we can leave it transparent
 props,←⊂'DrawMode'(2⊃State._mode)

 :For item :In arg ⍝ Verify, process & write each Text item one at a time
     '∆WI LENGTH ERROR: Text'##.Error~item≢⍛∊3 5
     '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Text'##.Error~##.IsNum at←2↑1↓item
     '∆WI RANK ERROR: Text'##.Error 2<|≡text←⊃item
     '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Text'##.Error~##.IsChar text
     points←tunits×at
     :If 2=≢⍴text ⋄ text←NL ##.∆sew ##.∆dtr¨↓text ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ A matrix - convert to vector with NLs
     text←ToChar text ⍝ Convert any numerics into plain characters
     text←↑NL ##.∆cuts text ⍝ Switch to a matrix to allow a multi-line property
     ⍝ Add a limiting size if they ask for it; use a Size pseudo-property
     State GUI props,('Text'text)('Points'points)('FontObj'State.FontObj),(5=≢item)/⊂'Size'(3↓item)
 :EndFor
